;; A sheltered hollow under a stepped roof; a steady lift (columns 4-6)
;; rises from its floor to Q. West of it the homeward shaft (D50) comes
;; down from Q beside the cliff, here two tiles thick (columns 0-1), to a
;; niche cut into it at (1,7)-(1,8), roofed by the cliff, a rock sill
;; (2,9)-(3,9) at its mouth: the rose stone is the niche's floor (1,9),
;; over a one-tile hole down to E. The way home, readable before H5 and
;; open with it: a glider steering west drops onto the sill and walks into
;; the niche, onto the stone. Shut, the stone seals the shaft: from E the
;; hole under it is the only cell that leads up, so nothing climbs past it
;; (the reverse route SYSTEMS' replay found when the shaft was open: wall
;; kicks up E's west wall into the shaft, then the lift).
;; test-cloudstair-homeward floods it.
(room
  region: cloudstair
  at: (7 -1)
  title: "Sheltered Seeds"
  intent: "seed creatures rest in a sheltered hollow below the last grass: a breath"
  bed: (wind 0.3 water 0 air 0.5 drone 0.3)
  light: 1
  sun: 1
  grid:
  ("##  ^^^##################"
   "##  ^^^   ###############"
   "##  ^^^     #############"
   "##  ^^^       ###########"
   "##  ^^^         #########"
   "##  ^^^           #######"
   "####^^^             #####"
   "####^^^                  "
   "####^^^                  "
   "#  o^^^ |  ||  |  | |    "
   "# #######################")
  things: ((seed at: (12 9) count: 3)
           ;; the shaft's rose stone (D50), the floor of the niche: shut,
           ;; the way home is sealed and nothing climbs up the shaft from E;
           ;; with H5 it opens as you step onto it, and you drop through
           ;; the hole under it to E
           (ring-stone at: (3 9) overtone: 5)
           (seed at: (5 5) count: 2))
  decor: auto)
